 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "SQLManager() starts empty. createTable(tableName, columnNames) creates a table (names are unique). insert(tableName, values) adds a row of strings: a value is an integer when it matches 0 or -?[1-9][0-9]{0,8}, otherwise a string. The first row stored in a table fixes each column's type; insert returns false (storing nothing) for a missing table, a wrong number of values, or a row whose value types differ from the fixed types, and true otherwise. select(tableName, conditions, orderBy, ascending) returns the stored rows (as their original strings, fresh lists) that satisfy every condition [column, op, literal] with op one of =, !=, <, <=, >, >=: integer columns compare numerically and a non-integer literal matches nothing; string columns compare by code points. orderBy \"\" keeps insertion order; otherwise rows are stably sorted by that column ascending or descending (ties keep insertion order). A missing table or a condition or order column that does not exist returns []. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
